;
; The lexical core of the plugin-hostd protocol, in ABNF (RFC 5234; %s"..." is a case-sensitive string, RFC 7405).
; It is written once, by hand. tools/abnf-gen.py appends to it the rules generated from the verb table
; (protocol/plugin-hostd-protocol.json): one rule per command, one per feedback line and one per parse refusal, and
; writes the whole as grammar/plugin-hostd-protocol.abnf.
;
; A message is one line of words separated by single spaces, the verb first. On the socket each message ends with a
; NUL byte (mod-host's framing), which is not part of the line. The library's parser compares the verb and counts the
; words; the types below are what a sender writes, and what the tests hold every line of the scenario corpus and every
; line the library answers to.

message          = request / answer / event

; a request is a command, and an answer a reply, each after a tag in a session that hello granted the extension tags:
; the answer to a tagged request starts with the request's tag. Without that grant a line that starts with "@" is a
; command whose verb no host has, answered "not found" as mod-host answers it. Feedback lines never carry a tag.
request          = [tag SP] command
answer           = [tag SP] reply
tag              = "@" 1*tag-char
tag-char         = ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / "."

; a feedback line, after its number in a session that hello granted the extension seq: 1 for the first line after that
; hello, one more for each line after it, so a number that is not one more than the last is a line the client missed
event            = [seq SP] feedback
seq              = "#" %x31-39 *DIGIT

; a reply: resp, the status, and the words the verb's reply grammar gives; or a parse refusal (generated, as
; protocol-error), which mod-host writes as the bare message
reply            = resp-line / protocol-error
resp-line        = %s"resp" SP status *(SP word)
status           = int

; the argument types of a format line: %i, %f and %s
int              = ["-"] 1*DIGIT
float            = ["-" / "+"] (decimal / non-finite)
decimal          = 1*DIGIT ["." *DIGIT] [exponent] / "." 1*DIGIT [exponent]
exponent         = ("e" / "E") ["-" / "+"] 1*DIGIT
; what param_info writes for a value that is not finite (NaN, Infinity, -Infinity), and what strtod takes, in any case
non-finite       = "nan" / "infinity" / "inf"
word             = quoted / bare-word
; a bare word: no space, no control character and no double quote
bare-word        = 1*bare-char
bare-char        = %x21 / %x23-7E / %x80-10FFFF
; a quoted word may hold spaces (a URI or a path); \" is a quote inside it, and the quotes are not part of the value
quoted           = DQUOTE *(escaped-quote / quoted-char) DQUOTE
escaped-quote    = %x5C DQUOTE
quoted-char      = %x20-21 / %x23-7E / %x80-10FFFF

; the tail of a format line that ends in ...: any further words
tail             = *(SP word)

; the words of a curve_bind after its instance and its display (doc/protocol.md, Curves), and curve_points' reply. The
; library reads the line by count as it reads any verb (cmd-curve-bind); these are the words a sender writes: clear, or
; the display's kind, its family and its terms, each <role>[.<index>]=<symbol>[:<unit>][@<shape>|<shape>...]. The role
; and shape words are omx-dsp's CURVE_ROLES and CURVE_SHAPES (omx_curve.h), held equal by tests/grammar_test.py; a
; family or a unit is a word, refused by its code when it has no closed form or its role does not take it
curve-binding    = %s"clear" / (curve-kind SP curve-family 1*(SP curve-term))
curve-kind       = %s"eq_response" / %s"transfer_curve"
curve-family     = 1*(%x61-7A / "_")
curve-term       = curve-role ["." curve-index] "=" curve-symbol [":" curve-unit] ["@" (curve-shapes / curve-slopes)]
curve-index      = 1*9DIGIT
curve-role       = %s"band_type" / %s"band_freq" / %s"band_gain" / %s"band_q" / %s"band_on" / %s"hpf_freq" /
                   %s"hpf_slope" / %s"hpf_on" / %s"lpf_freq" / %s"lpf_slope" / %s"lpf_on" / %s"threshold" /
                   %s"ratio" / %s"knee" / %s"makeup" / %s"range" / %s"knee_start" / %s"knee_end"
; a parameter's symbol; a host's own control starts with ":" (:bypass)
curve-symbol     = [":"] 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "_" / "-" / ".")
curve-unit       = 1*(%x61-7A)
curve-shapes     = curve-shape *("|" curve-shape)
curve-shape      = %s"off" / %s"bell" / %s"lowshelf" / %s"highshelf" / %s"highpass" / %s"lowpass" / %s"notch" / "-" /
                   %s"allpass1" / %s"allpass2"
; a head filter's slope, dB per octave of each choice value from 0: the role's declared enumeration
curve-slopes     = curve-db *("|" curve-db)
curve-db         = %x31-39 *2DIGIT
; curve_points' reply: the count and each point, x to four significant digits and y to 0.01 dB
curve-points-reply = %s"resp" SP %s"0" SP 1*DIGIT 1*(SP curve-point)
curve-point      = curve-x "," curve-y
curve-x          = ["-"] 1*DIGIT ["." 1*DIGIT]
curve-y          = ["-"] 1*DIGIT "." 2DIGIT
